{
	title: 'What a session changed: /changes and diffs on the web',
	spec: 'Each session keeps the files it changed, built from its file_changes records: per absolute path the first before and the latest after, so the list survives commits (a commit does not empty it). /changes lists them (path, +added -removed lines, which calls, undeclared ones marked, committed in <short hash> when a later reachable commit touching that path in that repo contains the path at exactly the after bytes, or its recorded deletion). Each path links to an authenticated web page showing the unified diff first-before to latest-after, with expandable steps per call; /changes/<session> has all its diffs, and ?path=<encoded absolute path> selects a recorded file, never an arbitrary host file. Pages name and link other sessions that observe the same absolute path. The terminal and web status row show the count of changed files ("7 files"), linking that page; the host pushes count updates after observations and clearing, without polling. Durable history marks retain the active file-change offsets and distinct paths, keeping status/snapshot reads independent of unrelated transcript length. /changes clear starts a fresh list using its durable command record; file-change records and blobs stay in history. Paths with no textual content show +? -? and explain undeclared, sensitive/large/non-regular or binary limitations, rather than inventing a diff. If the first observation has no content, first-before remains unknown; if the latest observation is undeclared, latest-after becomes unknown even when earlier bytes exist. Per-call steps still show captured diffs. Pages are read-only, no-store, escape paths and content, require the normal web login or terminal one-time code, wrap long paths/diff lines with one page scroller, use the host theme, support native links and at least 44px touch targets. Serving a page never blocks the host: every session\'s history marks (possibly rebuilt after an upgrade) are caught up in time slices (pages.slices) before the neighbour listing reads them.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Implementation: host/changes.ts aggregates observations and uses git diff --no-index against the existing SHA-256 file-blobs (no dependency or temporary copies). Changes pages are authenticated read-only HTML in host/changes-page.ts, routed before blob serving after the web gate. ?path selects only an aggregate record. Git history labels compare SHA-256 of committed raw bytes; Git timestamps have second precision, so the search starts at the observation second. Nonexistent/non-Git cwd simply yields no commit label. Sensitive/large and undeclared entries never fetch host bytes. Browser diff pages are request-time views, not polled; status counts push after observations and clear.',
		'pages.ts marks cache active observation offsets and changedPaths alongside its existing history indexes. Old marks rebuild to populate this index; status uses paths only, and diff listing reads just indexed file_changes records. /changes clear is the durable command boundary, not a new record type, so old file_changes stay readable and invisible to transcript/provider input.',
